# Samurai Linux sudo administration policy.
#
# Day-to-day work runs as an unprivileged user, and privilege is granted by the
# %sudo group that the installer creates - never by a shared root password, and
# never without one. install-test.py fails a release if any sudoers fragment on
# an installed system grants password-free root, so a live-session convenience
# rule could not quietly ride along into the copy on disk.
#
# These defaults tighten how the grant behaves:
#   env_reset            - the caller's environment cannot smuggle in PATH,
#                          LD_PRELOAD or locale tricks
#   timestamp_timeout=5  - a cached ticket expires before an unattended terminal
#                          becomes an open door
#   passwd_tries / timeout - a guessed password cannot be tried indefinitely
Defaults	env_reset
Defaults	timestamp_timeout=5
Defaults	passwd_tries=3
Defaults	passwd_timeout=60
